  "term": "illusory memory",
  "definition": "Illusory memory is a memory defect in which recollection is false or distorted, so a person seems to remember events or details that were not actually experienced or recalls them in a mistaken way. In this historical source, it is treated as a form of paramnesia, or false recollection.",
